#. TRANSLATORS: "Flesch Reading Ease" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:823
msgid ""
"Amstad is a recalculation of Flesch Reading Ease for "
"German text. It is meant for secondary and adult-level "
"text. Scores range from 0-100 (the higher the score, the "
"easier to read). Average documents should be within the "
"range of 60-70."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:859
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"#schwartz\">Schwartz German Readability "
"Graph</a> is designed for classroom instructional "
"materials."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:881
msgid ""
"This test is meant for secondary-age non-fiction "
"(specifically, 6-10 grade materials)."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:905
#: projects/base_project.cpp:928
msgid ""
"This test is meant for primary-age non-fiction "
"(specifically, light materials up to the 5th grade)."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:950
msgid ""
"German variation of Wheeler-Smith, which is meant for "
"primary-age reading materials."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:971
msgid "Rix (German fiction)"
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:972
msgid ""
"This test is a variation of Rix meant for German fiction "
"(specifically, grades 1-11)."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:998
msgid "Rix (German non-fiction)"
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:999
msgid ""
"This test is a variation of Rix meant for German non-"
"fiction (specifically, secondary-age to adult level "
"materials)."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1019
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1020
msgid "Lix (German children's literature)"
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1021
msgid ""
"This test is a variation of Lix meant for German "
"children's literature (specifically, grades 1-8). A <a "
"href=\"#german-lix-gauge\">chart</a> is also available to "
"visualize the score."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1043
msgid "Lix (German technical literature)"
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1044
msgid ""
"This test is a variation of Lix meant for German "
"technical/non-fiction literature. A <a href=\"#german-lix-"
"gauge\">chart</a> is also available to visualize the "
"score."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1067
msgid ""
"Qu is generally appropriate for secondary age (4th grade "
"to college level) readers."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1084
msgid ""
"A German adaption of SMOG, which is generally appropriate "
"for secondary age (4th grade to college level) readers. "
"SMOG tests for 100% comprehension, whereas most formulas "
"test for around 50%-75% comprehension."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1119
msgid ""
"SOL is meant for secondary-age (4th grade to college "
"level) Spanish reading materials. It is a modified "
"version of SMOG that was recalibrated for Spanish text."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1150
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"#GPMFryGraph\">Gilliam-Peña-Mountain graph</"
"a> is designed for most text, including literature and "
"technical documents."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1180
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"#FRASE\">FRASE graph</a> is designed for "
"educational materials (primarily Spanish as a secondary "
"language)."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1204
msgid ""
"The Crawford test is designed for primary-age Spanish "
"reading materials. A <a href=\"#crawford-graph\">chart</"
"a> is also available to visualize the score."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1226
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"#inflesz\">INFLESZ Scale</a> is a Flesch "
"Reading Ease like graph for Spanish. It is designed as a "
"general purpose formula for most text."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1264
msgid ""
"Harris-Jacobson is generally used for primary and "
"secondary age (Kindergarten to 11th grade) readers."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1289
msgid ""
"Spache is generally used for primary age (Kindergarten to "
"7th grade) readers to help classify school textbooks and "
"literature."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "New Dale-Chall" should not be translated; it is a test name.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1311
msgid ""
"New Dale-Chall is generally used for primary and "
"secondary age readers to help classify school text books "
"and literature."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1335
msgid ""
"PSK Dale-Chall is generally used for primary and "
"secondary age readers to help classify school text books "
"and literature."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1357
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"#FryGraph\">Fry graph</a> is designed for "
"most text, including literature and technical documents."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1388
msgid ""
"The <a href=\"#RaygorGraph\">Raygor estimate graph</a> is "
"designed for most text, including literature and "
"technical documents."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Degrees of Reading Power" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1423
msgid ""
"Degrees of Reading Power is designed for matching "
"documents to a student's reading ability (based on his/"
"her DRP score). This test is influenced by sentence "
"length, word length, and number of familiar Dale-Chall "
"words."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Degrees of Reading Power" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1448
msgid ""
"Degrees of Reading Power (GE) is designed for matching "
"documents to a student's reading ability (based on his/"
"her DRP score). This test is a conversion of a DRP "
"(difficulty) score into a grade level."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Bormuth Grade Placement" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1471
msgid ""
"Bormuth Grade Placement is designed for students and is "
"highly regarded for its accuracy because it uses three "
"variables (rather than the traditional two variables)."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Bormuth Cloze Mean" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1494
msgid ""
"Bormuth Cloze Mean is designed for students and is highly "
"regarded for its accuracy because it uses three variables "
"(rather than the traditional two variables)."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1516
msgid ""
"Wheeler-Smith is meant for primary-age (Kindergarten to "
"4th grade) reading materials."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Automated Readability Index" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1539
msgid ""
"Automated Readability Index, also known as \"ARI\" or "
"\"auto\", was originally created for U.S. Air Force "
"materials and was designed for technical documents and "
"manuals."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1562
msgid ""
"ELF is designed for \"listenability\" and is meant for "
"radio and television broadcasts."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Gunning Fog" should not be translated; it is a test name
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1580
msgid ""
"Gunning Fog is generally recommended for business "
"publications and journals."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "PSK Gunning Fog" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1614
msgid ""
"PSK Gunning Fog is generally recommended for business "
"publications and journals."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1632
msgid ""
"The Läsbarhetsindex (Lix) formula can be used on "
"documents of any Western European language. A <a "
"href=\"#lix-gauge\">chart</a> is also available to "
"visualize the score."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Rate Index" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1659
msgid ""
"The Rate Index (Rix) formula is a variation of Lix and "
"can be used on documents of any Western European language."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1685
msgid ""
"Coleman-Liau is meant for secondary age (4th grade to "
"college level) readers. This formula is based on text "
"from the .4 to 16.3 grade level range. This test usually "
"yields the lowest grade when applied to technical "
"documents."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1711
msgid "Danielson-Bryan 1 is designed for student materials."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1727
msgid ""
"Danielson-Bryan 2 is designed for student materials. It "
"is a variation of Flesch Reading Ease that uses character "
"counts instead of syllable counts. A <a "
"href=\"#DB2\">chart</a> is also available to visualize "
"the score."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1744
msgid ""
"FORCAST was devised for assessing U.S. Army technical "
"manuals and forms. It is the only test not designed for "
"running narrative, so it is mostly appropriate for "
"multiple-choice quizzes, applications, entrance forms, "
"etc."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Flesch Reading Ease" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1770
msgid ""
"Farr-Jenkins-Paterson is a variation of the Flesch "
"Reading Ease test, which uses the mono-syllabic word "
"count instead of the overall syllable count. Scores range "
"from 0-100 (the higher the score, the easier to read). "
"Average documents should be within the range of 60-70."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1789
msgid ""
"A modified version of Farr-Jenkins-Paterson designed for "
"U.S. Navy technical manuals and forms."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1806
msgid ""
"PSK Farr-Jenkins-Paterson is a variation of the Farr-"
"Jenkins-Paterson test, which returns a grade score "
"instead of a Flesch difficulty level."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Flesch Reading Ease" should not be translated.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1824
msgid ""
"Flesch Reading Ease is meant for secondary and adult-"
"level text and is a standard used by many U.S. government "
"agencies, including the U.S. Department of Defense. "
"Scores range from 0-100 (the higher the score, the easier "
"to read). Average documents should be within the range of "
"60-70. A <a href=\"#flesch-chart\">chart</a> is also "
"available to visualize the score."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1862
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1888
msgid ""
"Flesch-Kincaid is designed for technical documents and is "
"mostly applicable to manuals and forms, rather than "
"schoolbook text or literary works.\n"
"\n"
"This test is part of the Kincaid Navy Personnel "
"collection of tests."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "New Fog Count" should not be translated; it is a test name.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1908
msgid ""
"New Fog Count is a modified version of Gunning Fog "
"created for the U.S. Navy and was designed for technical "
"documents and manuals.\n"
"\n"
"This test is part of the Kincaid Navy Personnel "
"collection of tests."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1929
msgid ""
"The McAlpine EFLAW formula is used to determine the ease "
"of reading English text for ESL/EFL (English as a Second/"
"Foreign Language) readers. This test is influenced by "
"sentence length and words consisting of three or less "
"characters. To lower a score, try using shorter sentences "
"and longer, less colloquial words."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1949
#: projects/base_project.cpp:1981
msgid ""
"SMOG is generally appropriate for secondary age (4th "
"grade to college level) readers. SMOG tests for 100% "
"comprehension, whereas most formulas test for around "
"50%-75% comprehension."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:1980
msgid "SMOG (simplified)"
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "Modified SMOG" should not be translated; it is a test name.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:2001
msgid ""
"Modified SMOG is a variation of SMOG that is adjusted for "
"primary-age materials."
msgstr ""

#. TRANSLATORS: "New Automated Readability Index" should not be translated;
#. it is a test name.
#: projects/base_project.cpp:2018
#: projects/base_project.cpp:2038
msgid ""
"New Automated Readability Index is a modified version of "
"ARI created for U.S. Navy materials and was designed for "
"technical documents and manuals.\n"
"\n"
"This test is part of the Kincaid Navy Personnel "
"collection of tests."
msgstr ""

#: projects/base_project.cpp:2058
msgid "PSK Flesch is used for student readers."
msgstr ""

